---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_DESCRIPTION, SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <BaseHead title={SITE_TITLE} description={SITE_DESCRIPTION} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Header />
    <main>
      <section class="hero">
        <h1>Mutorium Labs</h1>
        <p class="tagline">
          Mutation testing for Web3 &amp; zero-knowledge systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          Mutorium explores how mutation testing can make smart contracts,
          zk-circuits, and cryptographic protocols more robust. The goal:
          help builders ship code that fails loudly in tests instead of
          silently in production.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/blog" class="button primary">Read the blog</a>
          <a
            href="https://github.com/mutorium"
            class="button secondary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            Explore the tools
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Why mutation testing?</h2>
        <p>
          Traditional tests tell you when something is broken. Mutation testing
          asks a deeper question: <strong>would your tests notice if the code changed in subtle ways?</strong>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Inject small “mutants” into your code or circuits.</li>
          <li>Run your existing test suite against them.</li>
          <li>See which mutants survive &mdash; and where your tests are blind.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article>
            <h3>Learning</h3>
            <p>
              Gentle introductions to mutation testing, coverage, and testing
              strategy for smart contracts and zk applications.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Research notes</h3>
            <p>
              Deep dives, experiments, and write-ups as we explore how mutation
              testing maps to EVM, Noir, and other ecosystems.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Tools</h3>
            <p>
              Open-source utilities and prototypes for metrics, coverage, and
              eventually full mutation testing pipelines.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>Services</h3>
            <p>
              Over time, Mutorium will offer focused reviews and testing
              engagements for teams that want to push quality further.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Stay in the loop</h2>
        <p>
          Follow along as the ideas, tools, and research around mutation testing
          in Web3 and ZK evolve.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            X / Twitter: <a href="https://x.com/mutoriumlabs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">@MutoriumLabs</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            GitHub: <a href="https://github.com/mutorium" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">github.com/mutorium</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
